Some VGA cards (for instance, the Vega Video Seven VGA card) contain 
non-standard VGA modes. If you are using one of these cards you might 
see graphics garbage where the dashboard of the car is supposed to be. 
To get rid of this garbage, insert your card's utility disk in drive A, 
locate the utility which disables the VGA extensions, and run this 
utility before beginning the game. The game will look OK then. 

As an example, the utility disk for the Vega Video Seven VGA card 
contains a utility called "vega". This utility contains several 
commands, one of which, called "pure", forces the card into true VGA 
mode. Before booting Street Rod, insert the utility disk in drive A 
and type A:VEGA PURE:ON and hit return. You will see a message that 
all extensions have been disabled. You can then start Street Rod and 
it will run as designed. You can also toggle dip switch 5 on the card 
to Off. This accomplishes the same thing. 
